---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<DocsLayout lang="en" title="Quick start" description="Connect the dashboard and your first agent in a few steps using the recommended Docker Compose installation.">
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Download the repository</h3>
      <p>The repository files include both Compose definitions and all sample configurations.</p>
      <CodeBlock lang="en" code={`git clone https://github.com/TheArchitect998/NodeSentinel.git
cd NodeSentinel`} />
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Register the agent in the dashboard</h3>
      <p>Copy the sample configuration and replace its name and key. Use a unique strong key of at least 16 characters.</p>
      <CodeBlock lang="en" title="nodesentinel.config.json" language="json" code={`{
  "agents": {
    "HomeLab1": {
      "mode": "push",
      "key": "ENTER_A_RANDOM_KEY_HERE"
    }
  }
}`} />
      <CodeBlock lang="en" code={`cp nodesentinel.config.example.json nodesentinel.config.json
chmod 600 nodesentinel.config.json
openssl rand -base64 32`} />
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Initialise the password and start the dashboard</h3>
      <CodeBlock lang="en" code={`docker compose pull
docker compose run --rm dashboard /usr/local/bin/nodesentinel dashboard setup
docker compose up -d
docker compose ps`} />
      <p>Then open <code>http://localhost:8888</code>. Use an HTTPS reverse proxy for access from the network.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Start the agent on a monitored host</h3>
      <p>Create a protected <code>.env</code> in the agent directory. The name and key must exactly match the dashboard entry.</p>
      <CodeBlock lang="en" title=".env" language="env" code={`NODESENTINEL_AGENT_NAME=HomeLab1
NODESENTINEL_AGENT_KEY=THE_SAME_RANDOM_KEY
NODESENTINEL_HUB_URL=wss://dashboard.example.com`} />
      <CodeBlock lang="en" code={`chmod 600 .env
docker compose -f compose.agent.yaml pull
docker compose -f compose.agent.yaml up -d`} />
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="callout warning"><strong>Secure it before enabling network access</strong><p>The Compose default binds the dashboard only to localhost. For remote access, use HTTPS and WebSocket support at the reverse proxy. Never transmit agent keys unencrypted across a network.</p></div>

  <h2>Verify the installation</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>The agent appears as online in the dashboard.</li>
    <li>CPU and memory metrics update.</li>
    <li>A test alert reaches the desired channel.</li>
    <li>Dashboard and agent configuration files cannot be read by other users.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
